From 0ea180783d1189ddf544465b0e3614abd2efa679 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Andr=C3=A9=20Machado?= <machaddr@falanet.org>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 11:30:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rtw89: keep the PineTab-V combo radio in USB 2 mode

Both PineTab-V schematics route the on-board RTL8852BU through the
USB 2-only GL850G hub. Only the module's USB_DP/DM pins are connected;
its SuperSpeed RX/TX pairs are unconnected.

The rtw89 USB probe now attempts USB 3 mode before registering the WLAN
interface. The AX mode-switch register write disconnects the USB device
and returns one, making probe skip core registration while waiting for
re-enumeration. This is unsuitable for this hard-wired USB 2 path and
also interrupts the Bluetooth interface on the same combo module. The
reported failure has no WLAN interface and includes a USB disconnect
alongside a failed Bluetooth register read.

Keep this radio in its supported USB 2 mode. Match the PineTab-V machine,
RTL8852B chip and GL850G parent USB ID together, so external adapters on
the tablet's USB 3 connector retain the existing mode-switch behavior.
Return zero before any switching register write, allowing the normal
USB 2 core registration and initialization to continue. Log this policy
so a physical boot capture can confirm that it was selected.

The GL850G USB ID is specified by the existing genesys,gl850g binding.
This removes a concrete mismatch with the board wiring; successful WLAN
scans and Bluetooth initialization still require physical validation.

Link: https://files.pine64.org/doc/PineTab/PineTab-V_Schematic_Ver1-20230614.pdf
Link: https://files.pine64.org/doc/PineTab/PineTab-V_Schematic_Ver2-20240730.pdf
Link: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/tree/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/genesys,gl850g.yaml?h=v7.3
Assisted-by: Codex (OpenAI)
---
 drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/usb.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/usb.c b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/usb.c
index aafa8b9..50a384f 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/usb.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/usb.c
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 /* Copyright(c) 2025  Realtek Corporation
  */
 
+#include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/usb.h>
 #include "debug.h"
 #include "mac.h"
@@ -1137,6 +1138,22 @@ static int rtw89_usb_switch_mode_be(struct rtw89_dev *rtwdev)
 static int rtw89_usb_switch_mode(struct rtw89_dev *rtwdev)
 {
 	struct rtw89_usb *rtwusb = rtw89_usb_priv(rtwdev);
+	const struct usb_device *hub = rtwusb->udev->parent;
+
+	/*
+	 * PineTab-V routes its RTL8852BU through a USB 2-only GL850G hub.
+	 * The module's SuperSpeed pins are not connected.  Switching modes
+	 * disconnects both WLAN and Bluetooth without a usable USB 3 path.
+	 * Match the on-board hub as well as the machine so external adapters
+	 * connected through the tablet's USB 3 connector retain auto-switching.
+	 */
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("pine64,pinetab-v") &&
+	    rtwdev->chip->chip_id == RTL8852B && hub &&
+	    le16_to_cpu(hub->descriptor.idVendor) == 0x05e3 &&
+	    le16_to_cpu(hub->descriptor.idProduct) == 0x0608) {
+		rtw89_info(rtwdev, "PineTab-V combo radio: retaining USB 2 mode\n");
+		return 0;
+	}
 
 	if (rtwusb->udev->speed == USB_SPEED_SUPER) {
 		rtw89_info(rtwdev,
